1
00:00:00,041 --> 00:00:01,750
[KARA] This is the point of life.

2
00:00:01,751 --> 00:00:03,545
Watching the sun rise…

3
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:05,004
…with the person you love.

4
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:07,006
I love you, Jao.

5
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:08,717
No matter what happens,

6
00:00:08,758 --> 00:00:10,427
always remember,

7
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:13,095
as long as the waves find their way back to shore,

8
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,305
I’ll always love you.

9
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:17,307
- [PEARL] Oh! Good day, sir! - Hello.

10
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:18,434
- Checking in? - Yes.

11
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:20,352
[PEARL] Well, welcome to Katig, sir.

12
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,979
Let me guess... Korean.

13
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:25,733
The owner of this hotel, my boss, he’s Korean, too.

14
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:26,735
[GUEST] Where is he?

15
00:00:27,026 --> 00:00:29,028
[HAN BIN SPEAKS KOREAN] Stop it already.

16
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,947
The guy you sent is trying to take me back!

17
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:31,906
Sir Han.

18
00:00:31,907 --> 00:00:34,576
We have a Korean guest and he wants to meet you.

19
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:35,493
What’s happening?

20
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:37,829
There’s a lot of things I need to tell you, but...

21
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:40,080
I never found the right opportunity.

22
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:41,290
I like you, Pearl.

23
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:42,292
A lot.

24
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:45,128
Wait, you’re confessing, but why does it feel like you’re—

25
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:46,254
[PEARL BREATHES DEEPLY]

26
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:47,588
you’re saying goodbye?

27
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:49,007
I won’t say goodbye.

28
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:50,216
[HAN BIN] I’ll see you again.

29
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:52,217
So? Does he have a chance with you?

30
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:54,637
[TANTAN] Hey, Pearl. I drove Sir Han earlier today.

31
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:55,472
To where?

32
00:00:55,473 --> 00:00:57,265
To the airport. T​​hey’re flying back to Korea.

33
00:00:57,307 --> 00:00:58,892
- [ARIEL] Huh? - Airport?

34
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,644
Sorry, Pearl.

35
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:04,939
Sir Han really is confusing.

36
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:09,985
He doesn't owe me an explanation.

37
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:11,780
So, it’s okay.

38
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,282
- [ARIEL] But don’t you think— - It’s okay, Ariel.

39
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,367
See you, Tantan.

40
00:01:17,702 --> 00:01:19,412
Pearl doesn't seem okay.

41
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:22,957
Tantan, she’s fine. Don’t worry.

42
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,168
Join us tomorrow at Cabitoonan, okay?

43
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,378
- We're planting mangroves. - Sure.

44
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:28,713
- See you! - Sir Handsome invited me, too.

45
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:29,547
Okay!

46
00:01:29,548 --> 00:01:31,174
- See you there! - See you!

47
00:01:36,721 --> 00:01:38,847
[ARIEL SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Good morning, Sir Noah!

48
00:01:38,848 --> 00:01:41,935
[ARIEL SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Good morning! Say hi to my vlog!

49
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:44,186
Good morning to all our viewers!

50
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:47,607
We're here today at <i>Barangay</i> Cabitoonan

51
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:50,234
for the first day of our planting ceremony

52
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:54,656
for our mangrove reserve extension.

53
00:01:54,864 --> 00:01:56,449
All right.

54
00:01:56,866 --> 00:01:59,493
Follow Pure Coast on social media!

55
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:00,995
Pure Coast is here.

56
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:02,664
Thank you, Pure Coast!

57
00:02:02,705 --> 00:02:04,082
Say hi to the vlog!

58
00:02:04,123 --> 00:02:06,709
Thank you, Pure Coast! Hello!

59
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:11,631
[SIARGAONON] Over here!

60
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:13,049
[ARIEL] How are you guys doing?

61
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:14,717
Too bad Sir Han isn’t here.

62
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,261
I wonder how his family is doing?

63
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:18,930
- [CAROL LAUGHS] - Princess Pearl sure misses him.

64
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:22,182
Oh, Princess Pearl.

65
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:25,687
All right! Let’s get planting! Time to focus!

66
00:02:25,728 --> 00:02:28,898
Let’s go! One, two, three! Let's start planting!

67
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:31,317
- [CAROL] Let’s go! - [CROWD CHEERING]

68
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:32,861
Let’s do the mangroves!

69
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:36,406
Yes! Because mangroves fight the letter B!

70
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:38,241
- B! - Bailing on us!

71
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:40,869
- Wrong answer! - It’s wrong?

72
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:43,538
Bad weather or floods! Not boys!

73
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,081
- Oh, Princess Pearl… - [ARIEL] Right.

74
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:48,376
- ...you’re in love. Right, Tantan? - Of course, Chona Mae.

75
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:50,419
Oh! Right? Who’s Chona Mae?

76
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:51,921
- [ARIEL] Chona Mae? - [YELPS] Who’s Chona Mae?

77
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:53,047
- [ARIEL LAUGHS] - Oh! Jeez.

78
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:55,007
[ARIEL] You don’t know Chona Mae, Mom?

79
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,633
- Uh... That’s Chona Mae. - Wrong.

80
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:59,137
Chona Mae, as in tsunami! Come on!

81
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:00,470
- [PEARL LAUGHS] Mom! - What kind of joke is that?

82
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:02,974
- You don’t know what a tsunami is? - Fine.

83
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:05,225
- [ARIEL] Mom, your age is showing. - Right, it’s a tsunami!

84
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:08,353
I’m getting tsunami’d here in the mangroves.

85
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:11,441
- [PEARL LAUGHS] - There! We can do this!

86
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:14,193
As long as we stick together here in the mangroves!

87
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:18,865
[ALON BY JL]

88
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:32,771
<i>"Such beautiful mangroves. Such a beautiful sight."</i>

89
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:35,483
Say hi to my vlog, Kara, Jao!

90
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:36,818
What’s up, vlog?

91
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:39,153
Egay, say hi!

92
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:43,657
[BACKGROUND CHATTER]

93
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:44,993
[JAO] Uh...

94
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:47,912
You know, Kara, you should plant the first mangrove...

95
00:04:48,287 --> 00:04:50,873
because this project won't be possible without you.

96
00:04:51,165 --> 00:04:53,458
Why me? This is everyone's project.

97
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:54,752
- [JAO] Come on. - [ARIEL] Kara, actually...

98
00:04:54,794 --> 00:04:57,255
[ARIEL] it's better if we show someone planting first.

99
00:04:57,296 --> 00:04:58,881
It will look better on video.

100
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,049
And it will raise awareness.

101
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:02,844
Let Egay do it. Egay.

102
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:04,886
- [JAO] Okay. - Go ahead and plant first.

103
00:05:04,887 --> 00:05:06,222
[EGAY] Why me?

104
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:09,350
Because what we’re doing here today is for you.

105
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,393
For the children of Siargao.

106
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:12,895
Go on, start planting.

107
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:17,442
[KARA] Give your mangrove a name, too.

108
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:20,111
[JAO] Already have a name in mind?

109
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:23,197
Need help naming it?

110
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:26,743
How about Jao? So you'll always remember me.

111
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:30,997
How about Karajao? Like your baby.

112
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:32,707
[ARIEL] A baby already?

113
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:34,666
- [ARIEL] Egay! - [JAO LAUGHS]

114
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:36,377
[ARIEL] You’re getting way ahead of yourself.

115
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:38,211
Karajao actually sounds nice.

116
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:39,421
Karajao… baby.

117
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:40,547
[ARIEL] Hmm...

118
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,549
Jao is fine.

119
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:43,592
- Just Jao, right, Egay? - [JAO CHUCKLING]

120
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:46,219
[ARIEL] Okay, everybody, look at the camera, okay?

121
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:49,139
On three, everyone say: Team Mangroves forever!

122
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,059
One, two, three—

123
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,602
[CROWD] Team Mangroves forever!

124
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:54,811
[CROWD CHEERING]

125
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:56,898
[CROWD CHANTING] Team Mangroves!

126
00:05:56,939 --> 00:05:57,523
[MAN] Let's go!

127
00:05:57,565 --> 00:06:00,234
[CROWD CHANTING] Team Mangroves!

128
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:02,235
- [JAO] Use both hands. There you go. - [KARA] There.

129
00:06:02,236 --> 00:06:04,238
- [ARIEL] There you go. - [JAO] Push it down first.

130
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:07,033
Then use this to…

131
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:10,953
[ARIEL] Kara, how are we going to plant all of these?

132
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:12,829
There's still so many!

133
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:13,623
[JAO] Oh!

134
00:06:13,624 --> 00:06:18,336
Tomorrow, some student volunteers from San Isidro are coming.

135
00:06:19,295 --> 00:06:20,712
And you didn’t tell me?

136
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:22,048
I wanted it to be a surprise.

137
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:26,844
Thanks. It really means a lot.

138
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,224
To… to everyone!

139
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:32,725
- To everyone? - The community...

140
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,977
the people of Cabitoonan... - [JAO] Oh.

141
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:37,020
- To Mother Earth... - To you...?

142
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:38,438
- Thank you. - To you, too?

143
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:41,733
- [ARIEL] Way to involve Mother Earth. - Come on, let's start planting!

144
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:44,070
[ARIEL] Okay. Let’s plant!

145
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:46,739
[ARIEL] KaraJao.

146
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:58,459
Song Ji Hoon.

147
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:01,671
Is this Sir Han?

148
00:07:05,049 --> 00:07:07,260
Chaebol…?

149
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:09,762
What’s that?

150
00:08:06,861 --> 00:08:10,239
[KARA] Don't think about Han Bin too much, he might bite his tongue.

151
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:14,535
I'm just researching mangroves.

152
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,122
[CAROL LAUGHS]

153
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:21,584
[ARIEL] So, tell me, what’s the scientific name of mangroves?

154
00:08:43,814 --> 00:08:45,358
Who did this?

155
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:04,584
[JAO] Kara!

156
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:06,587
- [JAO] Where are you going? - [KARA] The municipal office!

157
00:09:11,175 --> 00:09:13,344
[CAROL] What a shame.

158
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:15,972
Ma’am Vida!

159
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:18,641
[VIDA] Kara, I was just about to call you.

160
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,268
I heard what happened.

161
00:09:20,309 --> 00:09:21,602
Ma'am Vida, what happened?

162
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:23,604
Didn't your office already approve our project?

163
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:25,147
We have a permit!

164
00:09:25,189 --> 00:09:27,066
I know. And the permit is valid.

165
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:30,235
But we got a call from the new landowner.

166
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,237
New owner?

167
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:32,863
But there isn't any land left there, right?

168
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:34,198
The sea took it.

169
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:36,408
Didn’t we make it clear to your group?

170
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:38,035
The land where you want to plant mangroves

171
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:41,289
was once private property affected by sea level rise.

172
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,499
Therefore, it’s public domain now, right?

173
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,334
It belongs to the government!

174
00:09:45,376 --> 00:09:47,253
Yes, but under the law,

175
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:49,672
the previous owner still has priority

176
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:52,008
if they want to apply for an FLA.

177
00:09:52,883 --> 00:09:54,302
Foreshore Lease Agreement?

178
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:58,889
Yes, it's the agreement that lets you use land along the shore.

179
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:00,724
You just lease it from the government.

180
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:02,142
Why? Is there a development planned?

181
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:03,352
What are they building?

182
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:06,522
I can't give you that information because I don't know either.

183
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:08,065
Ms. Vida, please.

184
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:10,776
I know the previous landowner.

185
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:13,737
But they’re not the ones we’re dealing with.

186
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:15,947
We found out that

187
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:19,826
before the sea swallowed the land,

188
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:22,538
it had already been sold to a corporation.

189
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,625
I know how this will play out.

190
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:28,669
[JAO] I’ve seen this before.

191
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,177
For now, we need to find out

192
00:10:36,218 --> 00:10:39,013
who the previous owner sold the property to.

193
00:10:39,972 --> 00:10:42,141
Maybe, uh...

194
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:45,436
we can start there and offer them some alternatives.

195
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,521
Maybe the mayor can help us.

196
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:50,608
Noah said...

197
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:56,572
Pure Coast told him developers rarely give in to such mediations.

198
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:02,703
- [KARA SIGHS] - [JAO] We know there's a development,

199
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:05,206
but we don't know how big it will be.

200
00:11:06,123 --> 00:11:07,792
I mean, let’s face it.

201
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:12,463
Siargao is prime real estate for big developments now.

202
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:14,465
And that property is huge!

203
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:17,218
So a big hotel will definitely be built there.

204
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,808
It’s really disturbing how

205
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:28,312
these people see paradise and only think of profit.

206
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:32,108
They will destroy mangroves,

207
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:34,235
overbuild coastlines,

208
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:37,029
drain resources… And what?

209
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:40,116
Call it progress? Because they're making money?

210
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,035
When the ecosystem gets destroyed,

211
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:45,204
they won't be the ones who’ll suffer the consequences!

212
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:51,168
I'm sorry, okay? I don't mean to offend you.

213
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:53,421
And I don't mean to generalize...

214
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:55,964
- But surely there are some— - Wait. Kara.

215
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,758
You don’t have to apologize.

216
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,260
I understand you.

217
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:01,345
And your objections are valid.

218
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:03,431
[JAO SIGHS]

219
00:12:03,472 --> 00:12:04,974
It's just that...

220
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:08,351
I can already hear my boss's voice in my head, saying...

221
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:10,771
that everything is legal and aboveboard.

222
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:14,275
That this project will provide revenue for the local government

223
00:12:14,316 --> 00:12:15,693
and jobs for the people.

224
00:12:17,236 --> 00:12:20,239
Just because it’s permitted doesn’t mean it’s right.

225
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:22,366
Yes, it will provide jobs.

226
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:23,617
Temporarily.

227
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,120
At the end of the day, who'll suffer the consequences?

228
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:27,955
The next generation.

229
00:12:28,914 --> 00:12:32,001
And some ecosystems may not recover once they're damaged.

230
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:36,046
Don’t worry.

231
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:39,467
I’m with you in this fight.

232
00:12:41,343 --> 00:12:44,138
And I will fulfill my promise to Ruth…

233
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:46,515
and to you.

234
00:12:57,026 --> 00:12:59,445
It's nice to have someone fighting by my side.

235
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:10,247
[PHONE VIBRATING]

236
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:11,414
Let it be.

237
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:15,377
[PHONE CONTINUES VIBRATING]

238
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:18,547
[ARIEL] So...

239
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:22,842
[ARIEL SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Han Bin <i>oppa</i>'s real name is Song Ji Hoon!

240
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:26,055
- Song Ji Hoon? Song Ji Hoon. - Song Ji Hoon.

241
00:13:26,430 --> 00:13:29,016
[ARIEL SPEAKS SIARGAONON] No wonder he didn't like taking pictures

242
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:31,227
or videos with us.

243
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:35,022
Was he hiding from his family?

244
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:36,357
[SIARGAONON] For sure!

245
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:38,359
Because he's a chaebol, right?

246
00:13:38,526 --> 00:13:41,195
He's the heir to his family's business.

247
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:42,571
But...

248
00:13:42,613 --> 00:13:44,031
Isn't Han Bin <i>oppa</i>...

249
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:45,824
a free spirit?

250
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:50,412
He loves traveling and experiencing cultures.

251
00:13:50,454 --> 00:13:53,040
He wants to be free.

252
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:59,003
We've known him for so long now, right?

253
00:13:59,004 --> 00:14:00,339
[SIARGAONON] That's right.

254
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:04,760
And he never even trusted us enough to tell us the truth?

255
00:14:05,177 --> 00:14:07,263
If his father hadn't gotten sick,

256
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:09,890
or if he hadn't left, we would have never known, right?

257
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:12,726
[ARIEL] Because he was hiding from his family.

258
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:15,354
Whatever his reason,

259
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:18,481
it's probably for the best that he didn't burden us

260
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:20,693
- with hiding his identity. - [CAROL] That’s right!

261
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,571
Whatever Han Bin <i>oppa</i>’s reason was,

262
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:27,825
I'm just glad he chose to be treated like one of us!

263
00:14:27,866 --> 00:14:28,576
[ARIEL] Yeah.

264
00:14:28,577 --> 00:14:31,495
We got to see the real him.

265
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:34,540
- [SIARGAONON] That's right. - [CAROL] Hm.

266
00:14:36,166 --> 00:14:37,376
[PEARL SIGHS]

267
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:39,962
Hm...

268
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:45,258
Pearl.

269
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:46,719
[SIARGAONON] How are you?

270
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:49,388
[CAROL] Pearl!

271
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:51,181
Hm?

272
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:53,767
[SIARGAONON] Are you okay?

273
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:55,936
You miss him?

274
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:57,979
[ARIEL AND CAROL SQUEALING]

275
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,189
Hm?

276
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:04,152
[PEARL SIGHS]

277
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:06,446
I just want to know how he's doing, Mom.

278
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:07,448
[CAROL] Hm.

279
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:10,993
He seems to be going through something serious.

280
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,953
He hasn't even replied to my messages!

281
00:15:13,954 --> 00:15:16,080
Princess Pearl, he'll reply!

282
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:17,041
Yeah.

283
00:15:17,042 --> 00:15:19,500
You know there's a family emergency.

284
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:20,502
Right.

285
00:15:20,544 --> 00:15:23,755
Pearl, just like what Kara said,

286
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:26,383
[SIARGAONON] "He'll come back to Siargao."

287
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,510
You'll get to talk again.

288
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:30,220
[SIARGAONON] Yeah. That's right.

289
00:15:30,262 --> 00:15:31,472
Mhmm...

290
00:15:31,513 --> 00:15:32,598
Hm...

291
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:35,224
- Hm... - Hm...

292
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:35,934
Here.

293
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:37,478
[CAROL CHUCKLES]

294
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,232
[CAROL SIGHS]

295
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:54,244
[BROOM SWEEPING]

296
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:59,375
[NOAH] Looks like we won't get to see the mayor.

297
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:01,835
No. He'll talk to us.

298
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:03,712
Ma'am Vida said he's just busy.

299
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:05,047
Let's just wait.

300
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:07,174
[NOAH] You know, I really admire your resilience.

301
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:09,635
We have to keep fighting.

302
00:16:10,386 --> 00:16:12,096
Yup. It's exhausting.

303
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:16,308
But I think every fight helps us defend the environment better.

304
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:18,811
[STAFF] Kara, Noah. I'm sorry.

305
00:16:18,852 --> 00:16:22,898
The mayor can’t meet with you today due to an emergency meeting.

306
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,565
But come back tomorrow.

307
00:16:24,566 --> 00:16:26,276
Promise, I'll prioritize you guys.

308
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:28,612
[KARA] Okay. We’ll be here during flag ceremony.

309
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:29,571
- [STAFF] Okay. Sure. - Thank you.

310
00:16:29,572 --> 00:16:31,365
- [STAFF] Thanks. I’ll go to my meeting now. - Okay.

311
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:35,327
Kara, look at this.

312
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:12,488
Is there something you want to tell me?

313
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:14,323
How could you be the project head?

314
00:17:14,324 --> 00:17:15,617
Were you even going to tell me?

315
00:17:15,659 --> 00:17:17,369
But can you please trust me on this?

316
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:18,996
How can I trust you right now?

317
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:20,873
Do you hear yourself?

318
00:17:21,749 --> 00:17:24,375
‘Cause right now, you sound exactly like your boss.

319
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:26,086
[CAROL] Without those mangroves,

320
00:17:26,128 --> 00:17:29,715
the storm would have hit the island even harder.

321
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,634
[KARA] So please, come with me tomorrow.

322
00:17:32,676 --> 00:17:36,597
[KARA] Just think about it. Those trees aren't just trees.

323
00:17:36,638 --> 00:17:38,849
They're protecting our community.

324
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:41,059
And they're our legacy for the next generation.

325
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:41,894
[CAROL] Jao!

326
00:17:42,269 --> 00:17:44,479
This project can’t move forward, Jao.

327
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,688
Thanks to your company.

328
00:17:45,689 --> 00:17:47,941
I’m just being rational and professional about this.

329
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:48,983
[PAUL] Kara, right?

330
00:17:48,984 --> 00:17:50,986
I’m Paul. Jao’s boss.

331
00:17:51,653 --> 00:17:54,156
10 million. Name your price.
